      "scars_and_marks": null,
      "remarks": null,
      "details": "<p>On June 7, 1996, Mary Garcia Webb left her home in Wenatchee, Washington, on her way to visit family in\u00a0Conway, Arkansas. She was traveling with two known individuals when their vehicle broke down in\u00a0Livingston, Montana. Garcia continued by hitchhiking; someone came forward stating they had provided\u00a0a ride from Livingston, Montana to Billings, Montana.\u00a0 Garcia was last seen alive on June 8, 1996 off I-90, five miles south of Billings, Montana, around 4:30 p.m.\u00a0\u00a0On June 25, 1996, her body was found in Northeastern Wyoming, very close to the Montana state border.\u00a0\u00a0The victim had suffered multiple gunshot wounds and blunt force trauma.\u00a0\u00a0</p>\r\n<p><br />The Wyoming Division of Criminal Investigation is seeking information from anyone who may be able\u00a0to assist in this investigation.</p>",
      "caution": null,
      "description": "June 8, 1996\r\nBillings, Montana",
